    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented to make owner deletion a soft-delete.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. Entity \u2014 `model/Owner.java`**\nAdded a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, defaulting to `false`) with `isDeleted()` / `setDeleted(...)` accessors. A newly created owner is therefore `deleted = false`.\n\n**2. Database schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)\nAdded a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to the `owners` table. The tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column has to be declared in the SQL. (I placed `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL` \u2014 HSQLDB rejects the reverse order.) The default keeps existing seed rows at `deleted = false`.\n\n**3. OpenAPI spec \u2014 `openapi.yml`**\nAdded a `deleted` (boolean, `readOnly`) property to the `Owner` output schema. The generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` pick it up automatically, so GET returns the flag.\n\n**4. Controller \u2014 `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `deleteOwner`: instead of `clinicService.deleteOwner(owner)`, it now sets `deleted = true`, saves the owner, and returns `200 OK` with the owner body (2xx, record retained).\n- The create endpoint's **identity-key check**, **household-duplicate check** (`findHouseholdMembers`), and **soft possible-duplicate detection** (`findPossibleDuplicate`) now filter out owners with `isDeleted()`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n## Verification\n- `Cp46Tests` (both the soft-delete-retains-and-flags case and the deleted-owner-ignored-by-duplicate-check case): pass.\n- Full suite: **58 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nOne deliberate scoping note: per the spec (\"duplicate and identity checks must ignore deleted owners\"), I left the non-duplicate counters \u2014 per-city capacity, per-day cap, namesake count, and customer-code uniqueness \u2014 counting all rows including deleted ones, since those aren't duplicate/identity checks.",
